Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: pin qcom_fg registration against GCC pruning

CI GCC 16.1.1 dead-code eliminates the static qcom_fg_probe and the
module_platform_driver registration of the built-in CONFIG_BATTERY_QCOM_FG
fuel-gauge / battery driver at link time, so qcom-battery (the fuel gauge)
never binds and the charger cannot read battery status. This mirrors the
identical fix applied to qcom_smbx (0051): mark qcom_fg_probe __used and
replace module_platform_driver with an explicit __used device_initcall
(qcom_fg_init/qcom_fg_exit) anchored in the initcall section.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -1134,7 +1134,7 @@
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
 
-static int qcom_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+static int __used qcom_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct power_supply_config supply_config = {};
 	struct qcom_fg_chip *chip;
@@ -1357,7 +1357,16 @@
 	},
 };
 
-module_platform_driver(qcom_fg_driver);
+static int __used qcom_fg_init(void)
+{
+	return platform_driver_register(&qcom_fg_driver);
+}
+device_initcall(qcom_fg_init);
+
+static void __exit qcom_fg_exit(void)
+{
+	platform_driver_unregister(&qcom_fg_driver);
+}
 
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Caleb Connolly <caleb@connolly.tech>");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Joel Selvaraj <jo@jsfamily.in>");
